1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,070
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,280
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,720
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:16,730
I’m Jay.

6
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:18,170
Chan’s ex-girlfriend.

7
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:19,730
What are you thinking?

8
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,300
Why are you so sure
that you can do anything to me?

9
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:24,700
Because I know that you still love me.

10
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:26,900
She set the no-kiss rule with you, right?

11
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:30,000
It means you and Chan

12
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:32,689
are not at the stage
where I have to be worried.

13
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,300
You can scold me or act coldly towards me.

14
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,170
I’m okay with it.

15
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,570
But don’t chase me away
like I were an animal.

16
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:40,800
I’m also a human.

17
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:44,500
Mom.

18
00:00:46,090 --> 00:00:47,300
Let’s eat.

19
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,700
Today, we have chicken,
your favorite food.

20
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:54,900
I’ll feed you.

21
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:00,350
I don’t want to eat.

22
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,000
Please take a bite, Mom.

23
00:01:11,830 --> 00:01:13,100
I told you I don’t want to eat.

24
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,200
Do you want to eat something else?

25
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:23,490
How about fruits?

26
00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:25,650
Do you want to eat apples?

27
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:27,300
I’m not hungry.

28
00:01:27,630 --> 00:01:29,820
Why do I need to repeat myself, Key?

29
00:01:32,039 --> 00:01:34,780
You haven’t eaten anything
since yesterday.

30
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:37,200
Please eat something, Mom.

31
00:01:39,229 --> 00:01:40,470
You are just my daughter.

32
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:41,770
Don’t order me around.

33
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,500
Just let me die.

34
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:45,700
No.

35
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,979
Mom, please eat something.

36
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:48,800
No.

37
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:51,200
Please, Mom.

38
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:54,400
Get out.

39
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,370
Get out.

40
00:01:58,990 --> 00:02:00,770
But you haven’t eaten anything.

41
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:02,300
Get out.

42
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:06,400
Why are you still here? Get out!

43
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,000
-Get out.
-No.

44
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:10,000
Get out!

45
00:02:10,210 --> 00:02:11,260
No.

46
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,850
Get out. I told you to get out!

47
00:02:13,890 --> 00:02:15,400
No, get out!

48
00:02:16,570 --> 00:02:17,290
Mom.

49
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,400
Get out!

50
00:02:19,730 --> 00:02:20,700
Mom.

51
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,900
Get out. I told you to get out!

52
00:02:23,650 --> 00:02:24,600
Get out!

53
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:25,510
No, Mom.

54
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,670
No.

55
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:29,180
Get out!

56
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:31,100
Get out! Get out!

57
00:02:32,270 --> 00:02:33,300
Get out!

58
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:38,800
-Mom.
-Get out!

59
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:41,500
Get out!

60
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:45,200
-Get out!
-Pin.

61
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:48,900
Stop it.

62
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,000
-Stop it, Pin.
-Get out!

63
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:54,300
Get out!

64
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:56,680
Pin, what’s wrong with you?

65
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:57,900
She’s your daughter.

66
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:01,700
Why are you doing this to her?

67
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:06,600
Mom.

68
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:12,900
Mom.

69
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:19,900
-Take her out of here.
-Key, are you alright? Walk slowly.

70
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:23,700
Let’s go.

71
00:04:06,610 --> 00:04:07,800
How are you feeling?

72
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,800
Does it hurt a lot?

73
00:04:18,850 --> 00:04:21,300
The wound on my head doesn’t hurt much.

74
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,180
But it really hurts here.

75
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:31,600
It’s okay.

76
00:04:33,750 --> 00:04:35,100
If you feel hurt, just cry.

77
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:39,000
You have me.

78
00:04:41,730 --> 00:04:44,470
I know that Mom didn’t mean to hurt me.

79
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:50,500
But it really hurts, Peach.

80
00:04:52,550 --> 00:04:54,800
It hurts so much.

81
00:04:57,690 --> 00:04:58,900
It’s okay.

82
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,300
It’s okay.

83
00:05:10,470 --> 00:05:12,100
Key, you are not alone.

84
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,900
You still have me.

85
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:15,600
Come here.

86
00:05:16,770 --> 00:05:17,900
Cry as much as you want.

87
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,200
It will be alright.

88
00:05:26,890 --> 00:05:28,900
It’s okay. You have me.

89
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:47,600
I’ll take the monitor off.

90
00:06:53,150 --> 00:06:53,850
Mom.

91
00:06:55,159 --> 00:06:57,050
Why don’t you stay at the hospital
for a night?

92
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:59,900
No, I’m fine.

93
00:07:00,890 --> 00:07:02,290
But you passed out.

94
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,800
If Aunt Niam wasn’t there,
you would have fallen to the ground.

95
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,700
I’m just a little tired.

96
00:07:16,150 --> 00:07:17,100
Key.

97
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,700
Are you alright?

98
00:07:28,370 --> 00:07:30,000
Key, how did you know?

99
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,800
Peach called me.

100
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:36,800
She told me you passed out.

101
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:39,900
I’m okay.

102
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:42,000
I’ll feel better after getting some rest.

103
00:07:45,130 --> 00:07:47,500
Are you sure? I’m worried about you.

104
00:07:49,409 --> 00:07:52,400
I feel much better after seeing you.

105
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:39,270
(Hello.)

106
00:08:40,659 --> 00:08:41,700
(Hello, Chan.)

107
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,300
(Do you hear me?)

108
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:45,400
Yes.

109
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:47,900
(What’s up?)

110
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:54,900
Tonight,

111
00:08:56,290 --> 00:08:58,000
are you going to come to my condo?

112
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:04,800
I can’t.

113
00:09:06,210 --> 00:09:07,900
(I’m tied up with some family matters.)

114
00:09:10,150 --> 00:09:11,500
Is something wrong?

115
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:16,650
It’s nothing.

116
00:09:19,590 --> 00:09:20,950
Are you worried about me?

117
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,040
I’m just asking.

118
00:09:29,530 --> 00:09:32,100
That’s too bad.

119
00:09:33,470 --> 00:09:35,000
I thought you were worried about me.

120
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,950
You are joking with me now.

121
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,700
So you are no longer mad at me, right?

122
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:49,100
I don’t know.

123
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:51,700
Please take care of Simba for me.

124
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,500
Simba will soon forget you.

125
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:02,300
You didn’t come to visit him at all.

126
00:10:17,430 --> 00:10:18,370
Hello?

127
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:23,600
I’ll talk to you later.

128
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:28,800
Good night.

129
00:10:34,370 --> 00:10:35,150
Yeah.

130
00:10:48,550 --> 00:10:50,300
Your mommy is probably still mad at me.

131
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:55,500
What should I do to make up with her?

132
00:11:03,510 --> 00:11:05,200
Thank you for coming home.

133
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:08,250
Sorry for suddenly asking you
to come home.

134
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:12,400
I should be the one who apologizes.

135
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:14,360
I barely come home to visit Big Mom.

136
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,400
I told Aunt Niam to prepare your room.

137
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:21,200
If you need anything,
you can always tell me.

138
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:24,400
Yes.

139
00:11:24,650 --> 00:11:25,800
Thank you.

140
00:11:29,910 --> 00:11:31,400
I’m glad

141
00:11:32,870 --> 00:11:34,300
that you came home.

142
00:11:38,430 --> 00:11:39,200
Yeah.

143
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:43,500
Key.

144
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,600
No one can hurt you now.

145
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:49,300
I promise.

146
00:11:58,290 --> 00:11:59,200
I know.

147
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:02,480
Thank you, Peach.

148
00:12:05,010 --> 00:12:05,800
Go.

149
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:07,500
Go take some rest.

150
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,400
Good night.

151
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:17,350
(I told you not to come back.
Why did you come back?)

152
00:12:17,650 --> 00:12:18,800
(Why did you come back?)

153
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:25,300
(I was wrong.)

154
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:26,810
-(Why did you come back?)
-(I’m sorry.)

155
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:28,900
-(Didn’t I tell you not to come back?)
-(I was wrong.)

156
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:29,910
(I’m sorry.)

157
00:12:29,930 --> 00:12:31,000
(Why did you come back?)

158
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:34,970
Key.

159
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:35,900
Key.

160
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:37,630
Key. Key.

161
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:39,580
It’s okay, Key.

162
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:40,600
Come here.

163
00:12:41,610 --> 00:12:43,500
It’s okay. I’m right here.

164
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:45,800
It’s okay. It’s alright.

165
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,700
It’s okay.

166
00:12:48,890 --> 00:12:49,800
Key.

167
00:12:57,410 --> 00:12:58,800
It’s okay, Key.

168
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:00,800
There’s nothing to be scared of.

169
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,900
It’s nothing.

170
00:13:08,690 --> 00:13:10,600
No one can hurt you now.

171
00:13:12,770 --> 00:13:14,000
You have me.

172
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:26,900
It’s okay. Come here.

173
00:13:32,430 --> 00:13:33,900
I’m right here.

174
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:02,700
You can’t sleep, Key?

175
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,180
Big Mom.

176
00:14:09,110 --> 00:14:10,400
Why did you come out here?

177
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:12,100
You are still unwell.

178
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:21,800
I’m just like you.

179
00:14:22,450 --> 00:14:23,600
I can’t sleep.

180
00:14:32,770 --> 00:14:34,900
Today seems to be a good day.

181
00:14:36,950 --> 00:14:38,900
You came back home to see me.

182
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:42,200
It’s also the first quarter moon tonight.

183
00:14:46,730 --> 00:14:49,500
The first quarter moon?

184
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:50,500
Yes.

185
00:14:50,530 --> 00:14:55,370
It said that it’s the strongest phase
of the lunar cycle.

186
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:59,300
The moon reaches a 90-degree angle
from the Sun and the Earth.

187
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:15,300
It’s the phase where,

188
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:22,600
if you have the determination, hope,
or will to do something, you can succeed.

189
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:27,300
You can conquer burdens
and overcome your fear.

190
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:43,300
No matter what happens,

191
00:15:44,590 --> 00:15:49,000
you still have me, Peach, and your dad.

192
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:51,300
We always love you.

193
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:14,000
Thank you, Big Mom.

194
00:16:16,690 --> 00:16:18,000
I’m sorry

195
00:16:19,610 --> 00:16:21,500
for taking so long to come to visit you.

196
00:16:31,570 --> 00:16:33,070
I love you, sweetie.

197
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:37,950
I love you too.

198
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:00,100
Why are you leaving so soon?

199
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:01,700
Can’t you stay a bit longer?

200
00:17:04,319 --> 00:17:05,589
I have work to do.

201
00:17:05,630 --> 00:17:06,800
I can’t skip it.

202
00:17:07,060 --> 00:17:09,000
I also have an important errand to do.

203
00:17:10,170 --> 00:17:12,099
Why don’t you quit your job
and come to work for our family business?

204
00:17:12,619 --> 00:17:14,109
So you will have more free time.

205
00:17:14,150 --> 00:17:15,000
No.

206
00:17:15,230 --> 00:17:18,800
Asking me to quit singing is like
telling you to give up photographing.

207
00:17:21,079 --> 00:17:22,780
Now, you know how to talk back to me.

208
00:17:28,010 --> 00:17:28,950
Big Mom.

209
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,700
I’ll come to visit you more often.

210
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:34,970
Please take care of your health.

211
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:36,330
Yes.

212
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:40,850
Key, are you really not going
to have our chauffeur take you?

213
00:17:41,550 --> 00:17:45,000
I can have someone
take your motorcycle to your condo.

214
00:17:45,350 --> 00:17:46,720
I’m worried about you.

215
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,000
It’s okay, Big Mom.

216
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,900
Aunt Niam,
please take good care of Big Mom.

217
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:54,600
Sure.

218
00:17:55,010 --> 00:17:56,200
Don’t worry.

219
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:59,000
I’ll take good care of her.

220
00:18:00,110 --> 00:18:01,180
Great.

221
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:03,800
I’ve got to go.

222
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,700
I need to go to my condo to get changed.

223
00:18:07,250 --> 00:18:09,610
Let’s have a meal together next time.

224
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,920
I want to see Dad too.

225
00:18:12,850 --> 00:18:13,700
Yes.

226
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:19,000
I love you.

227
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,100
I’m leaving.

228
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:32,900
Bye.

229
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:36,180
Ride safely.

230
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,180
I will.

231
00:18:39,770 --> 00:18:41,050
Let me help you.

232
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:43,000
It’s okay. I can do it myself.

233
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:45,900
Okay.

234
00:18:47,850 --> 00:18:49,350
Thank you, Aunt Niam.

235
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:51,200
Ride safely.

236
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:53,300
Take care.

237
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:55,180
I’m leaving.

238
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:56,370
Bye.

239
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:58,400
I love you.

240
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,500
Love you too.

241
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:01,710
Please take care of her.

242
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,430
Ride safely.

243
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:17,160
She will come to visit you soon.

244
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,340
She’s really good on a motorcycle.

245
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:27,660
Don’t worry, Mom.

246
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:22,900
Chan.

247
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:27,600
Jay.

248
00:20:29,030 --> 00:20:30,100
Have you eaten?

249
00:20:34,950 --> 00:20:36,900
My restaurant launched
a soft opening today.

250
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:39,000
Can you go and taste the food?

251
00:20:42,530 --> 00:20:43,800
You should ask someone else.

252
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:45,500
I have work to do.

253
00:20:46,450 --> 00:20:48,100
You are the only one I want to ask.

254
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:53,200
Please.

255
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:55,900
Can’t you help me?

256
00:20:57,140 --> 00:20:58,970
You can help me as the hotel’s owner.

257
00:21:02,740 --> 00:21:03,900
And…

258
00:21:08,270 --> 00:21:10,150
I have an important thing to tell you.

259
00:21:11,750 --> 00:21:12,700
What is it?

260
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:16,250
Then come with me.

261
00:21:18,370 --> 00:21:19,200
Please.

262
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:21,300
I’m begging you.

263
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:28,270
Please give me another chance.

264
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:31,900
Please.

265
00:21:34,690 --> 00:21:36,000
Just one chance.

266
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:39,970
Let’s dine together, just the two of us.

267
00:21:43,490 --> 00:21:44,400
Please.

268
00:21:44,730 --> 00:21:45,500
Please.

269
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:49,700
Please.

270
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:51,350
Please.

271
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:03,890
Are you going out to eat?

272
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:11,700
Can I come with you?

273
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:20,600
I don’t remember inviting you.

274
00:22:24,260 --> 00:22:26,500
Jay, you are opening a restaurant.

275
00:22:27,290 --> 00:22:28,800
I’m sure you know that

276
00:22:29,570 --> 00:22:35,330
turning away your customer
is unprofessional.

277
00:22:44,180 --> 00:22:45,100
Okay.

278
00:22:46,290 --> 00:22:47,400
Well said.

279
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:52,800
But I’m sorry.

280
00:22:53,510 --> 00:22:54,800
I won’t let you come.

281
00:22:58,040 --> 00:23:02,900
Jay, do you feel intimidated by me?

282
00:23:09,580 --> 00:23:10,550
Fine.

283
00:23:14,690 --> 00:23:15,900
You can come.

284
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:26,700
I’m asking you two. Can you stop fighting?

285
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,700
We are not fighting.

286
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:36,700
Right, Jay?

287
00:23:48,970 --> 00:23:49,800
Yes.

288
00:23:51,870 --> 00:23:53,000
We are not fighting.

289
00:24:10,900 --> 00:24:12,400
You know a lot about food.

290
00:24:12,890 --> 00:24:15,570
Can you taste it and give me feedback?

291
00:24:19,950 --> 00:24:21,100
It tastes good.

292
00:24:21,730 --> 00:24:24,700
But I think it’s a bit too heavy
for the first course.

293
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:28,600
You said it like
you know a lot about food.

294
00:24:30,070 --> 00:24:31,350
I’m pretty good at it.

295
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:32,900
Stop it.

296
00:24:33,030 --> 00:24:34,100
Both of you.

297
00:24:36,740 --> 00:24:38,800
You said you have something to tell me.

298
00:24:39,420 --> 00:24:40,400
What is it?

299
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:42,700
You can tell me here.

300
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:49,130
No.

301
00:24:51,820 --> 00:24:54,800
I want to talk to you in private.

302
00:25:00,390 --> 00:25:02,120
Then we have nothing to talk about.

303
00:25:02,430 --> 00:25:03,400
I’m leaving.

304
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:08,700
I’m sorry

305
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:14,370
for leaving you to get married.

306
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:29,800
You’re sorry for leaving me
to get married?

307
00:25:37,750 --> 00:25:38,700
Yes.

308
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:42,100
This is all I can say.

309
00:25:50,730 --> 00:25:52,200
Can you forgive me?

310
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:02,640
Do you think that
your apology can fix everything?

311
00:26:03,050 --> 00:26:04,800
Do you expect me to go back to you?

312
00:26:06,140 --> 00:26:06,900
Jay.

313
00:26:07,690 --> 00:26:11,600
Your apology is just an empty word.

314
00:26:12,150 --> 00:26:14,100
It means nothing to me.

315
00:26:23,510 --> 00:26:24,500
I know

316
00:26:26,330 --> 00:26:28,440
that you were hurt when I left you.

317
00:26:32,730 --> 00:26:34,100
But my hands were tied.

318
00:26:35,910 --> 00:26:37,500
I had no choice.

319
00:26:40,380 --> 00:26:41,700
You had no choice?

320
00:26:44,030 --> 00:26:45,800
You had choices.

321
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:48,000
But you chose to leave me.

322
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,500
Whatever your reason was,

323
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:55,700
I’m not buying it.

324
00:28:33,890 --> 00:28:35,330
Don’t be sad, Chan.

325
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:39,500
Are you no longer mad at me?

326
00:28:42,310 --> 00:28:45,000
No. I’m not mad at you anymore.

327
00:28:51,180 --> 00:28:52,400
Is it that easy?

328
00:28:55,010 --> 00:28:56,000
Hey.

329
00:28:56,840 --> 00:28:58,300
I’m just your sugar baby.

330
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:00,000
I can’t stay mad at you for long.

331
00:29:00,600 --> 00:29:01,920
Otherwise, you might leave me.

332
00:29:05,700 --> 00:29:07,490
I really don’t understand you.

333
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:14,700
Come on. Don’t be stressed.

334
00:29:17,060 --> 00:29:18,100
So…

335
00:29:18,950 --> 00:29:23,120
I can sleep at your place tonight,
can’t I?

336
00:29:26,970 --> 00:29:28,100
Of course.

337
00:29:29,090 --> 00:29:31,300
Are you going to leave your son with me?

338
00:29:34,900 --> 00:29:35,800
You’re right.

339
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:39,400
I can’t leave our son.

340
00:30:16,590 --> 00:30:17,900
Can I have four shots of vodka?

341
00:30:18,380 --> 00:30:19,180
Serve them to me here.

342
00:30:19,210 --> 00:30:20,000
Yes.

343
00:31:47,560 --> 00:31:49,500
(Hello. Jay?)

344
00:31:49,860 --> 00:31:52,440
(I called you several times.
Why didn’t you answer my calls?)

345
00:31:56,130 --> 00:31:57,200
I’m busy.

346
00:31:57,890 --> 00:31:59,100
What did you call me about?

347
00:31:59,140 --> 00:32:00,170
(Where are you?)

348
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:01,300
It’s so loud there.

349
00:32:03,040 --> 00:32:05,200
Just say what you want.

350
00:32:06,920 --> 00:32:09,800
There’s a party at
Madam Ploy's this Saturday.

351
00:32:10,050 --> 00:32:11,340
You need to go.

352
00:32:11,380 --> 00:32:13,300
She hasn’t seen you for a while.

353
00:32:19,590 --> 00:32:21,200
Why do I have to go?

354
00:32:21,580 --> 00:32:23,400
We are not that close to her.

355
00:32:23,600 --> 00:32:26,630
(I told you to go, you just go.
Stop asking questions.)

356
00:32:26,670 --> 00:32:28,780
Can’t you do that for our family?

357
00:32:31,420 --> 00:32:32,900
For our family? Again?

358
00:32:33,920 --> 00:32:35,800
What I’ve done is not enough?

359
00:32:37,310 --> 00:32:40,090
Jay, don’t raise your voice at me.

360
00:32:40,130 --> 00:32:42,900
I’m doing all these things
for your future.

361
00:32:45,770 --> 00:32:46,800
For me?

362
00:32:48,410 --> 00:32:50,200
Or for yourself?

363
00:33:25,180 --> 00:33:27,200
Morning, Simba.

364
00:33:36,750 --> 00:33:38,350
Did your mommy wake up?

365
00:33:39,580 --> 00:33:40,780
Where is she?

366
00:33:59,200 --> 00:34:00,400
Do you want to watch the view?

367
00:34:01,350 --> 00:34:03,470
Let’s watch the view.

368
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:15,400
Let’s watch it together.

369
00:34:17,650 --> 00:34:18,800
I’ll put you down.

370
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:38,920
PLEASE FORGIVE ME. I MISS YOU SO MUCH.

371
00:34:40,810 --> 00:34:41,800
Chan.

372
00:34:54,290 --> 00:34:55,300
You’re up?

373
00:34:56,969 --> 00:34:58,600
How did you know that I’m up?

374
00:35:00,130 --> 00:35:01,400
I can sense it.

375
00:35:02,190 --> 00:35:04,500
I know everything about you.

376
00:35:06,740 --> 00:35:08,100
You are just guessing.

377
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:10,780
No.

378
00:35:11,810 --> 00:35:13,300
I spent a lot of time with you.

379
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:15,730
Now, I know your every move.

380
00:35:16,510 --> 00:35:18,260
I know what time you wake up.

381
00:35:18,590 --> 00:35:21,840
Even without an alarm clock,
you wake up at the same time every day.

382
00:35:23,420 --> 00:35:24,600
You sure know a lot.

383
00:35:25,930 --> 00:35:26,900
Of course.

384
00:35:27,990 --> 00:35:29,500
Because I’m your sugar baby.

385
00:35:35,910 --> 00:35:37,300
Do you want to have your breakfast now?

386
00:35:39,480 --> 00:35:40,400
Pepper?

387
00:35:46,040 --> 00:35:47,300
It looks tasty.

388
00:35:51,260 --> 00:35:51,970
Ouch.

389
00:35:53,940 --> 00:35:54,800
Key.

390
00:35:58,370 --> 00:36:00,400
Let me see. How is the wound?

391
00:36:01,300 --> 00:36:02,250
It’s okay.

392
00:36:02,700 --> 00:36:03,800
Let me take a look.

393
00:36:04,500 --> 00:36:05,570
It’s really okay.

394
00:36:05,610 --> 00:36:06,500
Key.

395
00:36:06,660 --> 00:36:07,930
It hurts.

396
00:36:08,420 --> 00:36:09,570
Let me see.

397
00:36:11,120 --> 00:36:11,900
Where is it?

398
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:16,850
My heart hurts.

399
00:36:18,590 --> 00:36:20,220
You hit me right in the heart.

400
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:22,050
It’s not funny, Key.

401
00:36:23,500 --> 00:36:26,600
Chan, I’m just kidding.

402
00:36:28,950 --> 00:36:30,100
Chan.

403
00:36:31,010 --> 00:36:32,900
Please don’t be mad at me.

404
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:35,120
I’m not good at making up.

405
00:36:36,180 --> 00:36:38,000
Chan, don’t be mad at me.

406
00:36:38,380 --> 00:36:39,900
Please, please, please.

407
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:46,450
Didn’t you say
you’re not good at making up?

408
00:36:47,630 --> 00:36:48,670
Yes.

409
00:36:49,100 --> 00:36:50,900
I’m not good at making up.

410
00:36:52,180 --> 00:36:54,200
But I’m good at something else.

411
00:36:56,850 --> 00:36:59,300
Who taught you these lines?

412
00:37:01,560 --> 00:37:03,500
I just can’t help it.

413
00:37:13,650 --> 00:37:14,900
Shall we start?

414
00:37:29,420 --> 00:37:30,900
Do you want to try the salmon?

415
00:37:41,330 --> 00:37:42,200
Come on.

416
00:37:43,070 --> 00:37:44,370
Aaah.

417
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:55,000
What will you have next?

418
00:37:57,850 --> 00:37:59,600
This or this?

419
00:38:03,430 --> 00:38:04,300
This.

420
00:38:07,670 --> 00:38:08,600
Fine.

421
00:38:20,090 --> 00:38:21,770
How is my skill?

422
00:38:27,270 --> 00:38:28,100
Good.

423
00:38:30,480 --> 00:38:32,560
I’m talking about my skill
from last night.

424
00:38:36,980 --> 00:38:38,100
You, little perv.

425
00:38:41,980 --> 00:38:43,100
Do you like it?

426
00:38:44,850 --> 00:38:46,280
I’m talking about the food.

427
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,100
Do you want another bite?

428
00:39:36,650 --> 00:39:37,800
I’ll help you put it on.

429
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:56,250
You smell good.

430
00:40:04,660 --> 00:40:05,900
I can do it myself.

431
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:10,500
Yes, you can.

432
00:40:11,670 --> 00:40:13,250
But it’s easier if I help.

433
00:40:37,030 --> 00:40:38,800
I’m always your girl.

434
00:40:44,190 --> 00:40:45,950
I want to be by your side

435
00:40:48,590 --> 00:40:50,530
and take care of you for a long time.

436
00:41:02,280 --> 00:41:04,100
It’s a business deal between us.

437
00:41:10,290 --> 00:41:12,900
As long as our deal
has not been cancelled,

438
00:41:15,260 --> 00:41:17,000
you can keep doing your job.

439
00:41:20,870 --> 00:41:22,000
What if…

440
00:41:23,500 --> 00:41:25,180
it’s not just a job?

441
00:41:26,050 --> 00:41:27,500
If…

442
00:41:29,070 --> 00:41:30,530
I really fall for you,

443
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:33,870
what will you do?

444
00:41:34,880 --> 00:41:37,840
♪ Your only one ♪

445
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:41,070
♪ I’ll make you love me,
make you remember ♪

446
00:41:41,510 --> 00:41:43,800
♪ I’ll keep repeating till you surrender ♪

447
00:41:43,950 --> 00:41:47,800
♪ With every touch, remember only me ♪

448
00:41:49,250 --> 00:41:51,260
♪ I’ll hold you close in everything I do ♪

449
00:41:51,910 --> 00:41:54,240
♪ Make it sink in, make you remember too ♪

450
00:42:08,430 --> 00:42:10,080
I heard that you went to my restaurant.

451
00:42:10,260 --> 00:42:11,400
How was the food?

452
00:42:11,760 --> 00:42:12,600
Was it good?

453
00:42:13,640 --> 00:42:14,600
I can’t tell.

454
00:42:15,130 --> 00:42:16,800
I ate only a little of it and left.

455
00:42:18,230 --> 00:42:19,100
Why?

456
00:42:19,610 --> 00:42:21,500
Didn’t Jay tell you why?

457
00:42:25,260 --> 00:42:26,100
Phu.

458
00:42:27,520 --> 00:42:29,800
Did Jay tell you to coax me again?

459
00:42:41,460 --> 00:42:43,100
Jay asked me to talk to you

460
00:42:44,620 --> 00:42:46,050
to persuade you to talk to her.

461
00:42:47,450 --> 00:42:49,270
She wants to explain

462
00:42:50,610 --> 00:42:52,160
why she broke up with you.

463
00:42:53,110 --> 00:42:58,000
Don’t you want to know
why Jay suddenly left you and got married?

464
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:05,200
No.

465
00:43:05,740 --> 00:43:09,200
Whatever her reason was,
it didn’t hold water.

466
00:43:09,240 --> 00:43:10,760
What is the point of knowing it?

467
00:43:12,710 --> 00:43:13,600
I know.

468
00:43:14,670 --> 00:43:16,400
Jay did a terrible thing to you.

469
00:43:17,880 --> 00:43:20,500
I also disappointed you.

470
00:43:21,330 --> 00:43:23,100
I’m saying this as your friend.

471
00:43:24,740 --> 00:43:26,800
I saw you’ve been hurt by this
for so long.

472
00:43:27,190 --> 00:43:28,000
Chan.

473
00:43:29,500 --> 00:43:31,180
Why don’t you hear her out?

474
00:43:31,690 --> 00:43:33,500
Not to forgive her.

475
00:43:34,150 --> 00:43:37,800
But for you to have your closure.

476
00:43:51,110 --> 00:43:52,900
You can tell Jay

477
00:43:53,790 --> 00:43:55,000
that I don’t want to hear it.

478
00:43:58,120 --> 00:43:59,100
You should leave.

479
00:44:00,040 --> 00:44:01,180
I have work to do.

480
00:44:51,120 --> 00:44:52,500
This is Chan and Key.

481
00:45:31,840 --> 00:45:32,700
Key.

482
00:45:37,650 --> 00:45:38,500
Jay.

483
00:45:42,380 --> 00:45:44,000
You can’t barge into my room.

484
00:45:44,710 --> 00:45:46,000
This is too much.

485
00:45:47,600 --> 00:45:49,200
You refuse to meet me.

486
00:45:49,620 --> 00:45:51,000
So I have to do this.

487
00:45:58,910 --> 00:46:00,700
You need to hear me today.

488
00:46:06,850 --> 00:46:08,650
Just say what you want to say.

489
00:46:17,230 --> 00:46:18,600
Do you remember Aunt Mon?

490
00:46:21,080 --> 00:46:22,900
My aunt who raised me

491
00:46:23,490 --> 00:46:25,100
after my parents died.

492
00:46:29,920 --> 00:46:31,000
The truth is…

493
00:46:33,250 --> 00:46:35,100
I’ve never had freedom in my life.

494
00:46:36,370 --> 00:46:39,500
(Jay, you know that
I’m having a problem right now, right?)

495
00:46:40,260 --> 00:46:41,400
Is it about money?

496
00:46:42,580 --> 00:46:46,300
My investment didn’t go
as well as I thought.

497
00:46:46,990 --> 00:46:48,600
Can you help me?

498
00:46:48,800 --> 00:46:51,500
I need money to put into the investment.

499
00:46:58,030 --> 00:46:58,780
Sure.

500
00:46:59,150 --> 00:47:00,570
I have some savings.

501
00:47:01,020 --> 00:47:02,460
I can give you 1 – 2 million baht.

502
00:47:02,500 --> 00:47:03,700
Jay.

503
00:47:04,890 --> 00:47:06,330
I need 10 million.

504
00:47:06,370 --> 00:47:07,430
10 million?

505
00:47:08,370 --> 00:47:10,520
Then you need to sell this house.

506
00:47:10,620 --> 00:47:13,520
This house has been passed down
from your great-grandfather.

507
00:47:13,560 --> 00:47:16,100
It belongs to our family.
How could I sell it?

508
00:47:16,380 --> 00:47:18,600
Then how will you find 10 million baht?

509
00:47:21,280 --> 00:47:23,000
Can you borrow it from Chan?

510
00:47:29,550 --> 00:47:32,700
You want me to borrow money
from my girlfriend to give it to you?

511
00:47:32,920 --> 00:47:34,080
Why not?

512
00:47:34,120 --> 00:47:36,930
Your girlfriend is the firstborn heir
of the Pattarasemsawats.

513
00:47:37,330 --> 00:47:40,640
Someone at her level
has the money to lend us.

514
00:47:41,190 --> 00:47:43,000
I will never borrow money from Chan.

515
00:47:43,040 --> 00:47:44,800
Why, Jay?

516
00:47:44,950 --> 00:47:46,800
I told you.

517
00:47:47,090 --> 00:47:50,840
Every relationship is transactional.

518
00:47:50,880 --> 00:47:53,500
It’s not embarrassing to admit it.

519
00:47:53,580 --> 00:47:55,800
But that’s not my relationship with Chan.

520
00:47:55,840 --> 00:47:57,800
It’s not true, Jay.

521
00:47:58,040 --> 00:48:01,570
When you are in a relationship,
you want love and desire from each other.

522
00:48:01,610 --> 00:48:03,970
You need to be able to depend on
and help each other.

523
00:48:04,070 --> 00:48:06,900
It provides mutual benefits
for both parties.

524
00:48:09,040 --> 00:48:09,730
Hey.

525
00:48:10,360 --> 00:48:14,000
Do you think
why I let you date her for this long?

526
00:48:14,320 --> 00:48:16,780
You have many rich men pursuing you.

527
00:48:17,340 --> 00:48:18,800
Do you think what my reason is?

528
00:48:20,250 --> 00:48:21,840
You also said that last month.

529
00:48:21,880 --> 00:48:23,800
How long do I have to wait?

530
00:48:23,900 --> 00:48:27,100
We’re talking about millions,
not just a couple bucks.

531
00:48:27,430 --> 00:48:29,940
If you can’t pay us back,

532
00:48:29,980 --> 00:48:31,530
you should get ready
to spend time in jail.

533
00:48:31,570 --> 00:48:34,250
I’ll find an investment fraud charge
against you.

534
00:48:34,310 --> 00:48:37,800
So people will know that the Homwarangkul,

535
00:48:38,550 --> 00:48:43,180
an old aristocratic family,
is actually a scammer.

536
00:49:03,960 --> 00:49:05,100
Aunt.

537
00:49:05,530 --> 00:49:06,350
Jay.

538
00:49:06,790 --> 00:49:08,240
What should I do?

539
00:49:08,280 --> 00:49:10,500
I didn’t mean it to end up like this.

540
00:49:11,360 --> 00:49:12,600
It’s okay, Aunt.

541
00:49:12,640 --> 00:49:14,000
We will work it out.

542
00:49:14,850 --> 00:49:15,700
Work it out?

543
00:49:16,700 --> 00:49:17,900
How, Jay?

544
00:49:18,760 --> 00:49:21,300
The only solution to help me,
you refuse to do it.

545
00:49:22,560 --> 00:49:25,000
If you agree to marry Derek,

546
00:49:25,540 --> 00:49:26,800
the problem will be solved.

547
00:49:28,870 --> 00:49:30,700
He is so crazy in love with you.

548
00:49:30,810 --> 00:49:33,500
He has everything
and is willing to help us.

549
00:49:42,220 --> 00:49:44,100
But I don’t love him.

550
00:49:45,420 --> 00:49:48,400
Then tell the person you love to help me.

551
00:49:49,230 --> 00:49:50,900
I’m your aunt.

552
00:49:51,260 --> 00:49:53,540
Aren’t you going to help me
when I have a problem?

553
00:49:57,730 --> 00:49:59,500
But this has nothing to do with Chan.

554
00:49:59,790 --> 00:50:01,760
These debts are not mine.

555
00:50:01,800 --> 00:50:03,900
What about the money that you spent?

556
00:50:04,100 --> 00:50:05,660
The money that I used
to support you through school.

557
00:50:05,700 --> 00:50:07,400
Where do you think it came from?

558
00:50:07,810 --> 00:50:08,480
Huh?

559
00:50:08,520 --> 00:50:10,400
Don’t be selfish, Jay.

560
00:50:10,740 --> 00:50:13,000
Who do you think got you
where you are today?

561
00:50:13,380 --> 00:50:14,400
Think about it.

562
00:50:14,760 --> 00:50:19,180
If I lived alone,
I wouldn’t need this much money.

